WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.647
Coding Exercise 5 is the main cardinality exercise in the assignment.

00:00:04.647 --> 00:00:07.372
The required grain is one row per patient.

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:11.797
You need an admission count, a lab count, and a prescription count,

00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:14.917
and patients with zero activity must still remain.

00:00:14.917 --> 00:00:19.067
Do not directly join all three detail tables and then count rows.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:23.312
That can create combinations and inflate the measures.

00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:29.302
Instead, summarize each child table by patient ID inside the provided common table expressions.

00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:33.932
Each summary should return one row per patient with one count.

00:00:33.932 --> 00:00:37.142
Then LEFT JOIN those summaries to patients.

00:00:37.142 --> 00:00:41.932
Use COALESCE so that a patient with no related activity shows zero instead of NULL.

00:00:41.932 --> 00:00:42.867
After Run and Check, validate the result.

00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:49.252
The number of output rows should equal the number of patients.

00:00:49.252 --> 00:00:53.347
Check a patient with several activities and a patient with no activity.

00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:58.097
This pattern is widely used when building dashboards and analytical feature tables.
